[Music]  [Applause]  hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan today I'm  going to ask a question from one of my  newsletter readers who wrote insane is  Albert what are the qualities for one to  become a successful businessman slash  entrepreneur so thanks for the question  Albert this is a really interesting one  so we have the greatest and largest  collection of famous entrepreneur  stories of any website online and if you  look at these famous entrepreneurs and  how they got started they have all sorts  of different personalities some of them  are type-a in-your-face really outgoing  and and social and others are introverts  and don't like talking to people and  there's no one common personality that  you have to have which is which I think  is good a lot of entrepreneurs or  startup entrepreneurs think they have to  be super outgoing or fit a certain mold  to be successful and it's not there's a  lot of guys who are shy and introverted  and still go on to build huge successful  companies so wouldn't works much of a  personality type but some of the things  the characteristics that these guys all  do have in common first they got started  you know a lot of people don't get  started they have a great idea and they  see other people  later on capitalize on it you got to you  got to do something about it right you  can't just sit as an employee at a  company come up with great ideas and  then get angry when somebody else goes  out and implements it you got to do it  yourself all these successful  entrepreneurs had an idea and they got  started they actually did something  about it they may not have jumped into  it full time right away but they did  something every day to grow their  business the next thing is you got to  have a really strong passion for what  you're doing starting a business is one  of the hardest things you ever gonna do  in your life it's gonna it's gonna it's  gonna be rough you know it's gonna test  you many times you're gonna think about  quitting many times and if you're just  in it for the money you're gonna give up  as soon as it gets really hard and I'm  talking really really hard you're gonna  quit because you don't really care that  much about it you're just trying to make  extra money and that's the wrong way to  approach it you want to approach it from  the perspective of doing something  you're really passionate about it and  you're helping people with and that is  the approach that that all the  successful entrepreneurs take and they  make money as a result because you're  providing a value-added product or  service but it comes from a place of  intense passion it's something that you  would do even if you weren't getting  paid to do because you love it so much  those are the things that you'll  continue doing with time to get really  really really hard so that's the second  thing I think about the next thing I  think about is just persistence a lot of  these guys the successful entrepreneurs  they're persistent they don't quit they  don't give up when things get really  really tough they still do something  every day even if it's small to grow  their business and move it forward  you can't quit you know it's it's again  gonna take way longer than you think  it's gonna take and be way harder you  think it's gonna be but you got to keep  going and the successful entrepreneurs  keep going until they see the light at  the end of the tunnel a lot of times our  chairs don't give it enough time to be  successful they put a ton of energy and  effort into it at the beginning they  don't allow for the momentum to grow and  then they quit because they don't see  things happening right away and didn't  they didn't allow for that time that  that it just takes to build the business  a lot of times so you gotta hit  something every day to keep it going and  the last thing I would say in terms of  characteristics of a successful  entrepreneur is stepping outside your  comfort zone we're really good at some  things everybody's different so you know  I'm really good at things that you're  probably not so good at and vice versa  and we tend to stick to the things that  we're really comfortable with and we're  really good at and not do the things  that we're not so good at and we're not  so comfortable with and and that's okay  you know as you as you build a business  you want to compliment your yourself and  have a team on board who can who can  help you when compliment the things that  you're you're bad at you know if you're  not a programmer I don't suggest going  out and becoming an all-star programmer  but you're gonna have to do things as  you grow your business to that stretch  yourself you know you have to stretch  you have to push outside your comfort  zone push outside your boundaries and  all the successful entrepreneurs did  that they did things that scared them  did things that they would normally do  because they really had this strong  intense passion to build this business  up and so your your goal  have to step outside your comfort zone  even if it's in small increments because  as it is chances are you don't have  enough to be able to build that business  so you're gonna have to become a better  version of you and and continue to  stretch yourself continue to grow  yourself especially if you want to build  a highly successful company so hopefully  that helped that's what I would suggest  and that comes from researching a whole  bunch of different famous entrepreneurs  and you can read their stories on the  website if you like those are you  watching if you liked the video please  give it a thumbs up below it always  makes me want to do more of these for  you and I love seeing them come in and  if you have a comment about this video  if you want to share your thoughts or if  you have a question about your own  business feel free to leave it in the  comment section below I always read  those always makes my day so thank you  I'd love to 